1. What is Helm in Kubernetes:
    - Helm is often called the package manager for Kubernetes.
    - It helps you:
        Install applications on Kubernetes easily
        Manage configuration
        Upgrade or rollback deployments
        Reuse deployment templates
    - Instead of writing dozens of raw YAML files manually, Helm lets you package everything into a reusable unit called a Helm Chart.

2. What is a Helm Chart:
    - A Helm Chart is a collection of Kubernetes YAML templates + configuration values.
    - Think of it like:
        Technology	Package Format
        Ubuntu	    .deb
        Node.js	    npm package
        Python	    pip package
        Kubernetes	Helm Chart
    - A chart can include:
        Deployments
        Services
        Ingress
        ConfigMaps
        Secrets
        Autoscaling
        Monitoring configs

3. Why Helm is Popular:
    - Without Helm:
        kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml
        kubectl apply -f service.yaml
        kubectl apply -f ingress.yaml
        kubectl apply -f configmap.yaml
    - With Helm:
        helm install myapp ./mychart
    - Helm handles:
        templating
        versioning
        upgrades
        rollbacks
        configuration overrides

4. Helm Architecture:
    - Components
        1. Helm CLI
            The command-line tool you use:
                helm install
                helm upgrade
                helm rollback
        2. Chart
            The application package.
        3. Release
            A running instance of a chart in the cluster.
        - Example:
            helm install prod-nginx bitnami/nginx
        Chart = bitnami/nginx
        Release = prod-nginx

5. Basic Helm Workflow:
    Add Repository
        helm repo add bitnami https://charts.bitnami.com/bitnami
    Update Repositories
        helm repo update
    Search Charts
        helm search repo nginx
    Install Chart
        helm install my-nginx bitnami/nginx
    List Releases
        helm list
    Upgrade
        helm upgrade my-nginx bitnami/nginx
    Rollback
        helm rollback my-nginx 1
    Uninstall
        helm uninstall my-nginx

6. Helm Chart Structure
    - Typical structure:
        mychart/
        ├── Chart.yaml
        ├── values.yaml
        ├── charts/
        ├── templates/
        │   ├── deployment.yaml
        │   ├── service.yaml
        │   └── ingress.yaml
        └── templates/_helpers.tpl
    
    - Important Files
        Chart.yaml
    - Metadata about the chart.
    - Example:
        apiVersion: v2
        name: myapp
        version: 1.0.0
        appVersion: "2.1"

    - values.yaml
    - Default configuration values.
    - Example:
        replicaCount: 2
        image:
            repository: nginx
            tag: latest
        service:
            type: ClusterIP
            port: 80

    - templates/
    - Contains Kubernetes manifest templates.
    - Example:
        apiVersion: apps/v1
        kind: Deployment
        metadata:
            name: {{ .Release.Name }}
    - Helm uses Go templating syntax:
        {{ .Values.replicaCount }}

7. How Templating Works
    If:
        # values.yaml
        replicaCount: 3
    And template:
        replicas: {{ .Values.replicaCount }}
    Generated YAML becomes:
        replicas: 3

8. Override Values
    You can customize installations.
    Using CLI
        helm install myapp bitnami/nginx \
            --set service.type=NodePort
    Using Custom Values File
        helm install myapp bitnami/nginx -f prod-values.yaml
    This is extremely common for:
        dev
        staging
        production

9. Helm + Kustomize
    - Since you asked earlier about Kustomize:
        Helm	                    Kustomize
        Package manager	            Overlay/customization tool
        Uses templates	            Pure YAML patches
        Great for reusable apps	    Great for environment customization
        Has chart repositories	    No package ecosystem
        More dynamic	            Simpler and Kubernetes-native
    - You can even combine them:
        Helm generates manifests
        Kustomize customizes them
    - Example:
        helm template myapp chart/ > output.yaml
    - Then apply Kustomize overlays.

